    {
      "id": "sdk-pkg-readme-errors",
      "scenario": "package-docs",
      "surface": "docs",
      "args": {
        "file": "@candledottv/agent-sdk/README.md"
      },
      "outcome": {
        "text": "Every non-2xx response throws `CandleApiError` with `code`, `status`, `retryable`, and\n(for field-level validation) `field`, plus `routing`, `discovery`, `coverage`, `uiHint` and\n`docsPath` when the envelope carries them. A refused build (`reason: \"presign_refused\"`) also carries `refusal` (the pre-sign check that fired) and `detail` (its sentence for why, for example that the price moved past `maxSlippageBps`) from 0.6.37; nothing was signed or sent, so it is safe to build again. `requestId` (SDK 0.6.38) is the API's\n`X-Candle-Request-Id` for the failed response, also on non-envelope errors, and the message ends with\n`(request id <id>)`: quote it when reporting a failed call, since it finds the exact log line. It is\nabsent from an older API. `REQUEST_ID_HEADER` and `requestIdOf(response)` are exported. Structured envelopes map straight through; the few\nlegacy endpoints without envelopes (activity, users) surface as `code: \"HTTP_<status>\"`. A\nSolana or EVM JSON-RPC failure throws `JsonRpcError`, with the RPC's numeric `code` and its\n`data` (for a failed simulation, `{ err, logs }`). The one-call write methods also put the\nidempotency id they sent on these errors, and wrap any other failure in `CandleOperationError`:\nsee \"Retrying a write that failed or timed out\" above. The full code table is on\n[Headless launch](https://docs.candle.tv/developers/headless-launch)."
      }
    },
